WEBVTT

00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:41.870
Let me say it just once, Chris.

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:46.040
I'm really scared, after all.

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:47.050
Yeah...

00:01:47.150 --> 00:01:48.920
It's funny, isn't it?

00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:50.950
I'm just a meta-body.

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:53.590
I'll be dead very soon, and yet...

00:01:53.590 --> 00:01:55.420
And yet, I'm still scared to die.

00:01:55.790 --> 00:01:57.430
It's not strange at all.

00:01:57.430 --> 00:02:00.560
Like Kyo Sogoru said, we're alive.

00:02:01.370 --> 00:02:04.960
You're alive and I'm alive, and both of
us have hearts which can feel pain.

00:02:06.740 --> 00:02:08.900
We're human.

00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:12.810
He's always so positive, isn't he?

00:03:01.390 --> 00:03:03.330
What?! Arque is?!

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:06.860
It's a shame.
She was a fine Cerebrant, but...

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:08.800
Oh, no.

00:03:09.670 --> 00:03:13.000
Her C.H.I.P. loss rate is now 1.748.

00:03:13.940 --> 00:03:16.530
It's amazing she can even maintain
her meta-body at this point.

00:03:17.110 --> 00:03:19.540
The dry damage and wet damage she has...

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:21.470
It's a whole order of magnitude
different from what we suffered.

00:03:22.010 --> 00:03:23.480
What are you saying?!

00:03:24.380 --> 00:03:26.320
With each transmission and reconstruction,

00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:30.020
large and small errors begin to present
themselves in our meta-bodies.

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:32.080
That's true for both you and for me.

00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:36.290
The errors affecting your
physical body is "dry damage."

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:38.760
Errors affecting your mind is "wet damage."

00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:42.290
Do they know about it? Does she know?

00:03:42.370 --> 00:03:42.890
Yes.

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:45.170
It's cruel.

00:03:45.170 --> 00:03:46.600
It just... offends me, somehow!

00:03:47.510 --> 00:03:49.370
Try not to be so sentimental.

00:03:49.370 --> 00:03:52.210
Our burden is about to get larger.

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:53.540
Be prepared.

00:03:53.810 --> 00:03:56.210
Sempai! Isn't that just a little coldhearted?!

00:03:56.950 --> 00:03:59.820
We're just hunks of data, so who
cares if one or two of us disappear?

00:03:59.820 --> 00:04:01.010
Is that what you're saying?!

00:04:02.550 --> 00:04:05.920
Arque... is the only friend I have.

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:18.600
I've decided.

00:04:19.700 --> 00:04:21.610
Yeah, And I've decided, too.

00:04:21.610 --> 00:04:24.040
You've decided? Decided what?

00:04:24.040 --> 00:04:24.800
That's a secret.

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:28.740
Okay, I'll keep my decision a secret, too!

00:04:35.050 --> 00:04:36.850
Why did you let Arque go out there?!

00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:39.550
It's just a normal recon mission.

00:04:40.260 --> 00:04:41.460
It won't be hard.

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:42.590
A recon mission?!

00:04:42.590 --> 00:04:44.260
We can do that!

00:04:44.330 --> 00:04:47.000
Why do you send Chris and Arque out on their own?

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:49.400
You've been doing it for days now!

00:04:50.140 --> 00:04:52.070
They asked to come here!

00:04:52.240 --> 00:04:55.570
You're trying to use them up before
the "expiration date," is that it?

00:04:55.710 --> 00:04:58.140
How could you?! That's just cruel!

00:04:58.280 --> 00:05:01.070
Well, Mr. President? Is that true?!

00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:05.780
Just wait a minute!

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:10.410
Kyo! Yehl!

00:05:10.520 --> 00:05:12.920
I received word from Arque.

00:05:12.920 --> 00:05:15.190
She wants to go to Maihama after they get back.

00:05:15.590 --> 00:05:17.530
Meet with her, will you?

00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:21.960
Meet with her? How do I even face her?!

00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:26.830
<i>What? You need me to be your cameraman?</i>

00:05:27.070 --> 00:05:29.110
I'm begging you, Kaminagi!

00:05:29.110 --> 00:05:32.770
Shizuno-sempai has some friends
visiting her that she met in France.

00:05:33.140 --> 00:05:34.980
So... How do I put this?

00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:38.080
I thought it'd be nice to get some
pictures to, you know, commemorate it.

00:05:38.080 --> 00:05:40.320
Maybe we shouldn't do this.

00:05:40.320 --> 00:05:42.620
Photos are just so... sentimental.

00:05:43.350 --> 00:05:45.520
What's so bad about being sentimental?

00:05:47.660 --> 00:05:52.130
I really wanted to get some
shots done for the movie today.

00:05:52.130 --> 00:05:53.500
<i>Nah, forget that!</i>

00:05:53.500 --> 00:05:56.430
<i>I'm the main character, so what's</i>
<i>the point if I'm not available?</i>

00:05:58.300 --> 00:06:00.500
<i>What? Is there still a problem?</i>

00:06:00.670 --> 00:06:02.900
Well, it's just...

00:06:02.970 --> 00:06:06.030
You basically want me to take some
pics of your double date, right?

00:06:06.410 --> 00:06:07.780
<i>Double date?!</i>

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:10.710
Am I wrong?

00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:14.820
They've arrived. Both of them.

00:06:27.500 --> 00:06:30.170
Okay, if this is a double-date...

00:06:30.170 --> 00:06:33.000
isn't this pairing off a little weird?

00:06:40.150 --> 00:06:42.610
They're both so pretty...

00:06:47.750 --> 00:06:48.340
Wha?!

00:06:53.360 --> 00:06:55.360
No way! You actually bought one?!

00:06:55.360 --> 00:06:55.720
Yup!

00:06:56.260 --> 00:06:57.360
It's a surprise.

00:06:57.360 --> 00:07:00.570
That's why she came to Maihama.

00:07:00.570 --> 00:07:03.600
Well, I've always wanted one, so...

00:07:03.600 --> 00:07:07.700
He looks just like the puppy I had in
my apartment back in Montparnesse!

00:07:08.140 --> 00:07:10.510
They're not easy to take care of, though.

00:07:10.510 --> 00:07:14.380
You have to feed a puppy four times a day!

00:07:14.380 --> 00:07:18.380
It'll be fine! Okay Chris,
what should we name him?

00:07:18.380 --> 00:07:19.250
A name, huh?

00:07:21.650 --> 00:07:24.820
Pieta... How about Pieta?

00:07:24.920 --> 00:07:29.380
I love it! That was the name of the
pub where you proposed to me!

00:07:30.130 --> 00:07:32.760
The quiche they served there was awful.

00:07:32.760 --> 00:07:34.390
So was the garçon's moustache!

00:07:37.100 --> 00:07:40.200
Here, Pieta! Say hello
to Mademoiselle Ryoko!

00:07:41.170 --> 00:07:44.400
Oh, he is just the cutest thing!
What'll I do?

00:07:46.880 --> 00:07:48.870
He's tickling me!

00:07:51.580 --> 00:07:55.080
I love this café.
It's like the other one, isn't it?

00:07:55.220 --> 00:07:58.760
Yeah. That café near the Seine, right?

00:07:58.760 --> 00:08:02.460
Let's get some cake together
when the next mission's over.

00:08:02.460 --> 00:08:04.490
We'll stuff ourselves till we're both sick!

00:08:04.600 --> 00:08:06.530
Right!

00:08:06.530 --> 00:08:09.300
I've never seen Shizuno-sempai
look so happy!

00:08:09.670 --> 00:08:13.260
Arque seems to be enjoying
herself, too. I'm glad we came.

00:08:18.880 --> 00:08:21.740
So, tell me.
How's it going with you and him?

00:08:22.380 --> 00:08:27.180
At least he has no trace
of the memories we shared.

00:08:27.720 --> 00:08:30.050
So, your old relationship with him is?

00:08:30.890 --> 00:08:34.150
Kyo saved me from the darkness.

00:08:34.290 --> 00:08:36.660
I still love him, even now.

00:08:37.430 --> 00:08:39.990
But he's been reborn.

00:08:40.330 --> 00:08:44.960
Now that he has, all I'd be is a witch
who'd cause him unhappiness.

00:08:45.740 --> 00:08:48.640
Oh, what is with this tragic
heroine act of yours?

00:08:48.640 --> 00:08:51.540
As always, you are the master
of doom and gloom!

00:08:51.540 --> 00:08:53.740
Figured you'd say that.

00:08:54.410 --> 00:08:58.010
When we first met,
I hated that gloomy face of yours!

00:08:58.150 --> 00:09:01.140
Like I hated that cheerful face of yours!

00:09:02.690 --> 00:09:06.520
Looks like there's a part
of you that still needs me!

00:09:07.390 --> 00:09:09.260
Yeah. You're right.

00:09:11.560 --> 00:09:14.190
It's okay. I still...

00:09:15.800 --> 00:09:17.630
I'll still fight.

00:09:18.400 --> 00:09:20.100
I want to fight.

00:09:21.540 --> 00:09:23.940
They started out so small.

00:09:23.940 --> 00:09:26.930
Back then, the Gards-orm
didn't even have a name.

00:09:27.110 --> 00:09:31.140
But they stole the lives and the
happiness of mankind away.

00:09:31.920 --> 00:09:34.390
By the time we awakened
within our server,

00:09:34.390 --> 00:09:36.420
the world had changed completely.

00:09:36.420 --> 00:09:38.190
That's why I'll fight.

00:09:38.190 --> 00:09:41.560
To regain our lives and our happiness,

00:09:41.560 --> 00:09:42.460
I'll fight the Gards-orm.

00:09:44.300 --> 00:09:45.600
A dog.

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:49.030
To transfer its data to the Oceanus...
That'll take a lot of time.

00:09:49.670 --> 00:09:51.570
I have a question.

00:09:51.570 --> 00:09:53.970
Why are you working
Chris and Arque so hard?

00:09:56.770 --> 00:09:59.270
Because I thought it'd be
best to keep them busy.

00:10:00.140 --> 00:10:02.940
To keep them from having
to think about the inevitable.

00:10:06.380 --> 00:10:09.980
Aw, stop it, Chris. You don't need to brag
about your wife to some high school kids!

00:10:10.790 --> 00:10:14.050
Can't help it!
My wife's my pride and joy!

00:10:14.130 --> 00:10:16.060
I'd like to tell you more about her.

00:10:16.060 --> 00:10:19.150
Yeah, but how are Kyo and
I supposed to take this?

00:10:22.330 --> 00:10:24.470
Something wrong, Kyo?

00:10:24.470 --> 00:10:26.440
Nothing. I'm fine.

00:10:27.640 --> 00:10:29.900
Let's enjoy ourselves.
For today, at least.

00:10:30.810 --> 00:10:32.610
It just doesn't feel natural.

00:10:32.610 --> 00:10:35.450
It's painful to look at.
Arque's smiling face...

00:10:35.450 --> 00:10:37.350
And you, Chris! Your smiles, too!

00:10:42.520 --> 00:10:45.090
The last thing I need is that dog.

00:10:45.090 --> 00:10:47.920
Is that her way of saying
"I'm not leaving you alone"?

00:10:48.060 --> 00:10:49.830
Should you be leaving her alone like this?!

00:10:49.830 --> 00:10:51.350
You should be with her now!

00:10:51.660 --> 00:10:53.250
It's fine.

00:10:56.300 --> 00:10:58.970
If we weren't doing this,
we'd be going out of our minds.

00:10:58.970 --> 00:11:02.170
While people are worried,
both Arque and I...

00:11:02.170 --> 00:11:04.510
can concentrate on them
instead of ourselves.

00:11:05.640 --> 00:11:08.940
Shizuno understands that,
which is why she's here for us.

00:11:11.680 --> 00:11:14.340
Sorry. That was thoughtless of me.

00:11:15.450 --> 00:11:17.490
You're perfectly nice, kid.

00:11:17.490 --> 00:11:19.320
Is there anything I can do for you?

00:11:19.990 --> 00:11:22.020
All you need to do is keep watching us.

00:11:23.590 --> 00:11:26.560
After the death of Paris and the
destruction of the Paris server,

00:11:26.560 --> 00:11:30.190
we became freelance mercenaries who
have wandered close to death many times.

00:11:30.540 --> 00:11:32.740
Giving up our lives wouldn't be
a tragedy at this point.

00:11:32.740 --> 00:11:34.670
The question is <i>how</i> we give them up.

00:11:34.670 --> 00:11:37.610
Where. When. And for whose sake.

00:11:43.210 --> 00:11:45.280
The way you're talking is!

00:11:45.280 --> 00:11:46.650
Don't misunderstand me.

00:11:47.050 --> 00:11:49.050
This isn't about Arque.

00:11:49.050 --> 00:11:51.390
I'm telling you about what
<i>I'm</i> prepared to do.

00:11:52.260 --> 00:11:55.090
Um... What have you guys
been talking about?

00:11:55.230 --> 00:11:57.190
Something very simple!

00:12:00.930 --> 00:12:04.770
Listen, you two. If there's someone you love,
then love 'em with all your heart!

00:12:04.770 --> 00:12:06.930
So you won't have any regrets later!

00:12:07.510 --> 00:12:09.130
R... Right...

00:12:12.040 --> 00:12:15.040
Wh-What's the big idea, Kyo?!

00:12:23.520 --> 00:12:26.560
Contact the Oceanus!
We've sighted the Viagem!

00:12:26.560 --> 00:12:27.550
Roger!

00:12:38.370 --> 00:12:39.930
Okay, that's got it!

00:12:40.510 --> 00:12:42.770
Thanks for coming today, Miss Kaminagi.

00:12:42.770 --> 00:12:45.040
It was a lot of fun, thanks to you.

00:12:45.040 --> 00:12:46.240
For me, too!

00:12:46.240 --> 00:12:48.510
I'll be sure to get the pictures to you.

00:12:48.510 --> 00:12:50.380
Please look at them, Miss Arque!

00:12:51.520 --> 00:12:55.320
Ryoko... I'm sorry, but could
you watch Pieta till the evening?

00:12:55.520 --> 00:12:56.150
Huh?

00:12:56.150 --> 00:12:58.160
Go to it, Kaminagi!

00:12:58.160 --> 00:13:00.530
I suppose so, but why?

00:13:00.530 --> 00:13:02.220
It's nothing. Nothing important.

00:13:02.330 --> 00:13:03.620
Could you, please?

00:13:03.860 --> 00:13:04.990
Sure.

00:13:07.800 --> 00:13:08.890
<i>We're coming back.</i>

00:13:13.600 --> 00:13:14.940
<i>All four of us will be back!</i>

00:13:22.950 --> 00:13:24.520
<i>This is a scramble!</i>

00:13:24.520 --> 00:13:26.950
<i>Attack target is the enemy</i>
<i>heavy transport Viagem!</i>

00:13:27.390 --> 00:13:30.880
<i>Their cargo is a disassembled deutera</i>
<i>zone main core which is in transit!</i>

00:13:31.020 --> 00:13:32.390
Which means?

00:13:32.390 --> 00:13:35.450
The main machine which
creates deutera zones.

00:13:36.030 --> 00:13:38.460
If we destroy it now,
it's one less attack for us to make.

00:13:38.830 --> 00:13:39.800
Are you sure?

00:13:40.060 --> 00:13:41.730
There's no doubt about it.

00:13:41.730 --> 00:13:44.760
All scanner data supports this conclusion.

00:13:45.000 --> 00:13:49.630
Commander. Arque's transmission
scatter rate is outside the permitted level.

00:13:50.410 --> 00:13:53.570
Her materialization probability
is only 89.63 C.C.A.T.

00:13:54.280 --> 00:13:55.770
It's not nearly enough
to maintain her meta-body!

00:13:56.510 --> 00:13:57.910
I'm really on the ball today!

00:13:58.420 --> 00:13:59.720
My body feels light!

00:13:59.720 --> 00:14:01.080
It does? Well, that's good.

00:14:03.620 --> 00:14:06.090
Level now up to 97.8.

00:14:06.460 --> 00:14:07.920
It's barely within maintenance levels.

00:14:08.560 --> 00:14:09.820
Transmit them!

00:14:10.560 --> 00:14:12.930
Commander, you can't do this!

00:14:12.930 --> 00:14:15.300
You can't send her out in this condition!

00:14:15.300 --> 00:14:16.770
It's what Arque wants!

00:14:18.440 --> 00:14:23.500
If she can't be saved, she wants to
serve humanity till the very end!

00:14:24.110 --> 00:14:25.340
She told me that herself.

00:14:26.310 --> 00:14:27.280
<i>Countdown, started!</i>

00:14:28.110 --> 00:14:30.170
<i>Transmission scatter rate, confirmed!</i>

00:14:30.750 --> 00:14:33.420
The Garuda's Q.L. isn't going
to last much longer.

00:14:33.420 --> 00:14:36.610
Equip holonic weaponry as soon
as you transmit! Assist them!

00:14:37.320 --> 00:14:38.850
<i>Chamber seal, released!</i>

00:14:39.420 --> 00:14:41.520
<i>Moving to transmission chamber.</i>
<i>All green.</i>

00:14:41.790 --> 00:14:43.890
Materialization coordinates, set and locked!

00:14:44.230 --> 00:14:45.490
<i>Zegapain, transmit!</i>

00:14:46.100 --> 00:14:47.120
Entangle!

00:15:04.720 --> 00:15:06.550
We've knocked out its main generator!

00:15:06.550 --> 00:15:07.710
Take care of the rest!

00:15:07.950 --> 00:15:09.720
Right! We're on it!

00:15:19.800 --> 00:15:21.320
Dammit! It's not going down!

00:15:29.510 --> 00:15:31.130
Chris! It's headed your way!

00:15:37.880 --> 00:15:39.610
Chris, what's wrong?! Arque!

00:15:42.990 --> 00:15:43.950
CHRIS!

00:15:44.620 --> 00:15:49.030
Shizuno. Kyo. We're through fighting.

00:15:49.930 --> 00:15:50.550
Hey!

00:15:50.960 --> 00:15:51.760
Chris!

00:15:53.700 --> 00:15:56.930
Chris... Where are you? Chris...

00:15:57.740 --> 00:16:00.570
It's come.
The moment we've dreaded...

00:16:01.570 --> 00:16:04.470
But I won't let you go by yourself!

00:16:11.480 --> 00:16:13.040
Banishment mode, activated!

00:16:13.150 --> 00:16:16.090
Hraesvelg will self-destruct in 180 seconds!

00:16:16.550 --> 00:16:17.350
What?!

00:16:17.350 --> 00:16:19.060
Self-destruct?!

00:16:19.060 --> 00:16:20.830
Q.L. charge is overloading!

00:16:20.830 --> 00:16:23.090
The limiter has been manually deactivated!

00:16:23.690 --> 00:16:26.990
I think he's trying to increase the
explosive power of when it self-destructs!

00:16:27.160 --> 00:16:29.130
Execute a forced recovery of the pilots!

00:16:29.130 --> 00:16:30.900
The circuits have been cut!

00:16:30.900 --> 00:16:32.500
I can't even contact them.

00:16:32.500 --> 00:16:34.630
Every approach from
the Oceanus has been blocked!

00:16:35.170 --> 00:16:36.230
No!

00:16:36.410 --> 00:16:38.770
He wants to take himself out
along with the Viagem!

00:16:39.380 --> 00:16:41.040
To die with Arque!

00:16:42.410 --> 00:16:44.310
I've made my decision.

00:16:44.980 --> 00:16:48.540
I can't imagine a future without Arque.

00:16:49.120 --> 00:16:51.350
Don't do this, Chris! Don't do this, please!

00:16:57.930 --> 00:16:59.600
Chris, stop this!

00:16:59.600 --> 00:17:01.960
Do you think Arque would be
happy that you're doing this?!

00:17:02.230 --> 00:17:04.220
I don't want to think about it.

00:17:05.100 --> 00:17:06.870
I have too many deaths on my hands.

00:17:07.200 --> 00:17:08.340
Chris!

00:17:08.340 --> 00:17:10.070
<i>Hurry up and clear out of here!</i>

00:17:10.070 --> 00:17:12.410
It's a question of how I lay down my life.

00:17:12.410 --> 00:17:15.470
I've decided it's going to be here and now.

00:17:16.610 --> 00:17:19.140
Quit laying on that BULLSHIT!

00:17:19.450 --> 00:17:22.540
<i>I don't know when or if I'm gonna die!</i>

00:17:22.990 --> 00:17:25.220
But you're wrong about this!

00:17:26.160 --> 00:17:28.420
I'm glad you took those pictures.

00:17:29.060 --> 00:17:31.890
Arque and I will be able to live on in them.

00:17:32.360 --> 00:17:33.850
SHUT UP!!!

00:17:38.900 --> 00:17:41.370
Kobrals! Abyss and Sin!

00:17:42.810 --> 00:17:46.240
But how?! Didn't Chris destroy them before?!

00:17:46.810 --> 00:17:49.910
The Gards-orm can reproduce
them from stored data!

00:17:50.210 --> 00:17:51.040
What?

00:17:51.520 --> 00:17:55.350
They can be physically reborn again
and again as Reconstructants!

00:17:55.850 --> 00:17:58.320
That's why they don't fear pain or death!

00:18:07.230 --> 00:18:10.360
It's fate. My final prey shall be you two.

00:18:11.200 --> 00:18:15.470
That transmission failure happened
while Arque was fighting you.

00:18:15.970 --> 00:18:18.270
The ones who did this to Arque...

00:18:18.580 --> 00:18:21.270
It was you! ABYSS! SIN!

00:18:29.250 --> 00:18:30.880
Damn!
I can't turn and face them!

00:18:39.600 --> 00:18:41.460
Now die, Abyss!

00:19:06.590 --> 00:19:10.390
Feed Pieta for me every day, won't you?

00:19:11.460 --> 00:19:13.020
A... Arque...

00:19:13.460 --> 00:19:16.560
If you ever forget...
I'll never forgive you.

00:19:25.880 --> 00:19:28.900
Won't you let me die with you?

00:19:30.650 --> 00:19:32.450
I made my own decision.

00:19:34.080 --> 00:19:36.290
You can't let me have peace?!

00:19:36.290 --> 00:19:39.620
You'd have me live on alone
and carry on in torment?!

00:19:40.930 --> 00:19:43.390
YOU AREN'T ALONE!!!

00:20:05.680 --> 00:20:07.050
Chris! Get out of there!

00:20:24.100 --> 00:20:24.660
Got 'em!

00:20:35.450 --> 00:20:39.310
I'd like one last taste... of café au lait...

00:20:54.030 --> 00:20:55.770
Chris...

00:20:55.770 --> 00:20:56.770
What, Dear?

00:20:56.770 --> 00:21:00.500
What should we name the puppy?

00:21:00.770 --> 00:21:03.430
Pieta. Would you like that?

00:21:03.940 --> 00:21:05.700
I... love it...

00:21:19.560 --> 00:21:20.550
Arque.

00:21:23.690 --> 00:21:26.930
<i>Your battle is over now... Arque.</i>

00:21:35.640 --> 00:21:39.470
Arque's data cluster...
It can't be reconstructed.

00:21:40.380 --> 00:21:43.440
She was a professional,
right to the very end.

00:21:43.980 --> 00:21:47.750
The retreat path the Kobral took probably
leads to the Gards-orm main base.

00:21:48.490 --> 00:21:50.890
We may be able to pinpoint its location.

00:21:51.390 --> 00:21:54.790
Always so cool and calm,
aren't you, Commander?

00:21:55.290 --> 00:21:59.700
If my tears could bring Arque back to life,
I'd be crying as hard as I could.

00:22:02.430 --> 00:22:03.300
Yes, sir.

00:22:08.440 --> 00:22:10.810
You're kidding. Miss Arque is?!

00:22:12.040 --> 00:22:14.770
She was ill. For a long time.

00:22:19.450 --> 00:22:20.510
Oh, Kyo!

00:22:34.060 --> 00:22:35.660
<i>I...</i>

00:22:36.030 --> 00:22:38.300
<i>I love you, Kaminagi.</i>

00:22:51.580 --> 00:22:54.310
From one of the protected to a protector.

00:22:55.020 --> 00:22:59.180
It's not known if Ryoko Kaminagi
will develop as a Cerebrant or not.

00:22:59.760 --> 00:23:03.860
But the beautiful things
and the cruel things...

00:23:03.860 --> 00:23:07.130
When she wants to see
the truth with her own eyes,

00:23:07.700 --> 00:23:10.390
what will you do then, Kyo Sogoru?

00:23:11.440 --> 00:23:14.630
Next time, on Zegapain: "The Awakened."

00:23:15.340 --> 00:23:18.010
My thoughts, never to be erased.
